WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.122
The assembled graph is a declarative version of the same bounded algorithm.

00:00:07.122 --> 00:00:10.912
The normal path is start, retrieve, grade, generate, end.

00:00:10.912 --> 00:00:17.537
The corrective path is retrieve, grade, rewrite, then retrieve again.

00:00:17.537 --> 00:00:26.951
And there is a safe failure path: grade, stop, end when evidence remains weak and the correction budget is exhausted.

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:29.907
That safe stop is important.

00:00:29.907 --> 00:00:35.622
The graph should not force generation from evidence it already judged insufficient.

00:00:35.622 --> 00:00:42.142
The advantage of the graph representation is that transitions are easier to inspect and extend.

00:00:42.836 --> 00:00:51.118
Later, you can add persistence, streaming, checkpoints, human approval, or another tool without hiding the control flow

00:00:51.118 --> 00:00:53.493
inside one large while loop.
